UNITS = [{'id': 'PEDS-U161', 'ch': 20, 'n': 1, 'title': 'TORCH — General Aspects (Transmission, Trimester, Manifestations)', 'sec': 'TORCH Infections · p86', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-001', 'PEDS-C20-002', 'PEDS-C20-003', 'PEDS-C20-004', 'PEDS-C20-005', 'PEDS-C20-006', 'PEDS-C20-007', 'PEDS-C20-008', 'PEDS-C20-009', 'PEDS-C20-010', 'PEDS-C20-011', 'PEDS-C20-012', 'PEDS-C20-013', 'PEDS-C20-014', 'PEDS-C20-015'], 'guide': 'TORCH Intrauterine infection transmitted from mother to baby: Toxoplasmosis; Others: Syphilis, Zika virus, Parvo B19 virus; Rubella; Cytomegalovirus (CMV); Herpes simplex. Type of maternal infection 1. Primary (mother infected during pregnancy; m/c transmitted) 2. Secondary/reactivation (Latent infection reactivation; Transmission of syphilis, CMV). Time of gestation 1st trimester m/c (Organ anomalies, ↑ risk congenital anomalies, Highest transmission risk). Common manifestations Antenatal IUGR m/c, IUD, Preterm delivery, Abortions; Postnatal Bone marrow suppression (Anemia, thrombocytopenia), Hepatosplenomegaly, Lymphadenopathy, Jaundice/abnormal LFT (Subclinical).'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U162', 'ch': 20, 'n': 2, 'title': 'Congenital Rubella Syndrome (CRS) — Triad, Features, Diagnosis, Management', 'sec': 'Congenital Rubella Syndrome · p86', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-016', 'PEDS-C20-017', 'PEDS-C20-018', 'PEDS-C20-019', 'PEDS-C20-020', 'PEDS-C20-021', 'PEDS-C20-022', 'PEDS-C20-023', 'PEDS-C20-024', 'PEDS-C20-025', 'PEDS-C20-026', 'PEDS-C20-027', 'PEDS-C20-028', 'PEDS-C20-029', 'PEDS-C20-030', 'PEDS-C20-031', 'PEDS-C20-032'], 'guide': 'CRS Severe maturation infection. Clinical Triad Heart defects (PDA, Pulmonary artery stenosis PS, VSD), Sensorineural hearing loss (SNHL) m/c, Cataract. Other features 1. Salt and pepper retinopathy (Black and white spots on retina; m/c ocular finding) 2. Blueberry muffin lesion (Purpuric spots non-blanching dome-shaped papules; severe CRS; dermal erythropoiesis; non-specific). Chronic manifestations 1. Progressive rubella panencephalitis (PRP) school going age, similar to SSPE (measles) poor scholastic performance, seizures, intellectual impairment 2. Adult-onset Diabetes 3. Hypothyroidism. Diagnosis Fetal IgM antibodies against rubella (maternal IgM cannot cross placenta); IgG not used (maternal IgG crosses placenta). Management No treatment (damage permanent); Prevention immunization of parent (during their childhood).'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U163', 'ch': 20, 'n': 3, 'title': 'Congenital CMV — Transmission, Triad, Diagnosis, Treatment', 'sec': 'Congenital CMV · p87', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-033', 'PEDS-C20-034', 'PEDS-C20-035', 'PEDS-C20-036', 'PEDS-C20-037', 'PEDS-C20-038', 'PEDS-C20-039', 'PEDS-C20-040', 'PEDS-C20-041', 'PEDS-C20-042', 'PEDS-C20-043', 'PEDS-C20-044', 'PEDS-C20-045', 'PEDS-C20-046'], 'guide': 'Congenital CMV m/c TORCH infection. Transmission rate 3rd trimester (90%) → Organogenesis complete → Asymptomatic; 1st trimester → Organogenesis incomplete → Congenital cytomegalic inclusion disease. Triad Microcephaly, Chorioretinitis, Intracranial calcification (periventricular). Other SNHL (m/c long term sequelae; m/c cause of non-syndromic hearing loss in children), Rash (Petechiae d/t ↓ platelets; Blueberry muffin lesion), Hepatosplenomegaly. Diagnosis PCR (Urine > blood > saliva; Screening; as early as possible); Serology (Low sensitivity) IgM antibodies against CMV. Treatment Ganciclovir IV 6 weeks → Oral 6 months; Goal prevent progression neurological disorders, decrease risk of SNHL in future.'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U164', 'ch': 20, 'n': 4, 'title': 'Congenital Toxoplasmosis — Triad, Diagnosis, Treatment', 'sec': 'Congenital Toxoplasmosis · p88', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-047', 'PEDS-C20-048', 'PEDS-C20-049', 'PEDS-C20-050', 'PEDS-C20-051', 'PEDS-C20-052', 'PEDS-C20-053', 'PEDS-C20-054', 'PEDS-C20-055'], 'guide': 'Transmission risk highest in 3rd trimester. Triad Hydrocephalus (unique), Chorioretinitis, Intracranial calcification (Diffuse calcification). Other Low IQ, Deafness (SNHL), Some cases A/W microcephaly. Diagnosis Serology IgM/IgA ELISA (more sensitive), Immunosorbent agglutination assay (ISAGA) test; PCR in CSF/tissue sample (if neurological involvement +). Treatment Infected child All cases symptomatic and asymptomatic should be treated: [Pyrimethamine + Sulfadiazine x 1 year] + [Folic acid (To prevent bone marrow suppression cause by Rx)]; Infected mothers Spiramycin ↓ transmission risk.'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U165', 'ch': 20, 'n': 5, 'title': 'Congenital and Perinatal Varicella', 'sec': 'Congenital Varicella Syndrome · p89', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-056', 'PEDS-C20-057', 'PEDS-C20-058', 'PEDS-C20-059', 'PEDS-C20-060', 'PEDS-C20-061'], 'guide': 'Congenital Varicella Syndrome Intrauterine transmission of herpes zoster; Period of risk 2nd trimester (13-20 weeks of gestation). Clinical 1. Cerebral atrophy 2. Microcephaly 3. Limb hypoplasia 4. Cicatrix (Irregular scarring, resembles burn scar). Perinatal Varicella more common than congenital varicella; Period of highest risk 5 days before to 2 days after delivery; Management immediately after birth Varicella zoster > IV Ig (Prevention); If lesions (+) Acyclovir.'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U166', 'ch': 20, 'n': 6, 'title': 'Congenital Syphilis — Early and Late Features, Management', 'sec': 'Congenital Syphilis · p89', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-062', 'PEDS-C20-063', 'PEDS-C20-064', 'PEDS-C20-065', 'PEDS-C20-066', 'PEDS-C20-067', 'PEDS-C20-068', 'PEDS-C20-069', 'PEDS-C20-070', 'PEDS-C20-071', 'PEDS-C20-072', 'PEDS-C20-073', 'PEDS-C20-074', 'PEDS-C20-075', 'PEDS-C20-076', 'PEDS-C20-077', 'PEDS-C20-078', 'PEDS-C20-079', 'PEDS-C20-080', 'PEDS-C20-081'], 'guide': "Unique feature Recurrent Abortion; Period of risk >4 months of gestation (≥ 2nd trimester). Early onset <2 years 1st Rhinitis (Snuffles) 2nd Vesiculobullous rash palms and soles (Pemphigus syphiliticus) 3rd Bone (metaphysis, Osteochondritis, Periostitis) → Bone pain, If severe Pseudo paralysis + Edema of affected limb (Soft tissue shadow on xray). Late onset >2 years 1. Hutchinson's triad (SNHL, Interstitial keratitis, Hutchinson's teeth notching/peg shaped incisors) 2. Mulberry molars (Irregular surface d/t rudimentary cups; usually 1st molar) 3. Deformed nose (Preceded by Saddle Nose deformity; Perforations; bony deformities) 4. Rhagodes (Fissures around mouth/nose) 5. Saber shin (Bowing of tibia) 6. Clutton's joint (B/L knee effusion). Management Diagnosis VDRL (baby and mother) 4 fold ↑ titres diagnostic; Treatment Aqueous crystalline penicillin/Penicillin G > 3rd generation cephalosporin: Ceftriaxone."}, {'id': 'PEDS-U167', 'ch': 20, 'n': 7, 'title': 'Congenital Zika Virus Infection', 'sec': 'Congenital Zika · p90', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-082', 'PEDS-C20-083', 'PEDS-C20-084', 'PEDS-C20-085', 'PEDS-C20-086', 'PEDS-C20-087', 'PEDS-C20-088', 'PEDS-C20-089'], 'guide': 'Vector Aedes aegypti mosquito → Infected mother → Baby; Period of risk 1st trimester. 1. Skull manifestations Partial collapse of skull, Internal abnormalities (Overlapping of sutures), Brain damage (Microcephaly, Hypertonia/spasticity, Extrapyramidal chorea/athetosis, D/t basal ganglionic damage, Occipital prominence). 2. Limb manifestations Abnormally curved limbs (d/t multiple contractures); Arthrogryposis multiplex congenita. 3. Eye manifestations Coloboma, Pigmentary retinal mottling, Scar + in macula. 4. Others SNHL.'}, {'id': 'PEDS-U168', 'ch': 20, 'n': 8, 'title': 'Congenital Parvovirus B19 Infection', 'sec': 'Congenital Parvovirus B19 · p91', 'qs': ['PEDS-C20-090', 'PEDS-C20-091', 'PEDS-C20-092', 'PEDS-C20-093', 'PEDS-C20-094'], 'guide': 'Transmitted across all trimesters; most sensitive period of transmission 2nd trimester. Tropism for erythroid lineage (Primarily at the pronormoblast stage). Clinical 1. Severe anemia → High output cardiac failure 2. Direct cytopathic effects on myocardium → Myocarditis; Fetal cardiac arrest → IUD (Intrauterine death) 3. Non immune hydrops fetalis.'}]

